2025-10-08 12:30:44,754 [WARNING] Skipped idx=474: gold or llm supporting sentence is empty. gold='', llm='The TAp73 isoform, also known as p73α, is one of the two main isoforms of the p73 protein in humans, the other being the N-terminally truncated ΔNp73 (p73β). Both isoforms are products of alternative splicing from the TP73 gene. The TAp73 isoform includes the full-length 126 kDa protein that contains both the N-terminal and C-terminal regulatory domains. This isoform is involved in various cellular processes, including cell cycle regulation, apoptosis, and maintenance of epithelial cell polarity. It has been shown to suppress epithelial-to-mesenchymal transition (EMT), a process associated with cancer progression, by downregulating E-cadherin and upregulating β-catenin, thus affecting cell adhesion, migration, and proliferation. In three-dimensional cultures, TAp73 knockdown in MCF10A cells, which are a model of mammary epithelial cells, leads to disruption in cell polarity, forming irregular acini without hollow lumen, and induces EMT as evidenced by the downregulation of E-cadherin and upregulation of β-catenin and laminin V. Additionally, TAp73 knockdown increases the expression of Snail-1, Slug, and Twist, EMT inducers that repress E-cadherin, leading to a more aggressive phenotypic change in the cell.'
